 "narrative": "The PTEN follow-up materially strengthens the reversed PTEN association. In TP53-loss-intact lines, H58/R42 gives a signed mean difference of +0.259 composite units with 95% interval +0.169 to +0.349, so the raw PTEN-loss contrast is lower composite, i.e. stronger measured dependency, and the interval is entirely beyond the 0.15-unit threshold in the claimed direction. I accept H58. In the triple-negative TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4 stratum, H51/R44 gives +0.252 [+0.169,+0.335], also fully above threshold and therefore strong conditional evidence that the PTEN-loss association is not absorbed by the three dominant predictors. I accept H51. By contrast, H59/R43 in TP53-loss-positive lines is +0.102 [-0.187,+0.391]; the cells are small and the interval is broad, so this stratum remains unresolved and deferred. I request independent validation for H58 rather than H51 because H58 is larger and tests whether the new PTEN signal survives in a broad TP53-intact stratum while retaining more power; H51 remains accepted as supportive conditional evidence.\n\nCDKN2A remains borderline and likely subthreshold. H57/R41 in TP53-intact lines gives +0.125 [+0.051,+0.199], and H52/R45 in the triple-negative stratum gives +0.144 [+0.083,+0.204]. Together with H19/R33 (+0.141), the estimates are directionally consistent but not decisive: point estimates are below 0.15 and lower bounds are well below it. I keep H57 and H52 unresolved but deferred rather than active, because additional follow-up on this endpoint has lower priority than PTEN validation and remaining predictor screens.\n\nThe research_signature_a>=1 interaction tests are mostly negative for the originally claimed amplification. H60/R46 tests SMARCA4-loss amplification in high signature_a and gives -0.008 [-0.174,+0.157], effectively null; H61/R47 tests KEAP1-loss amplification and gives -0.060 [-0.254,+0.134], also null/small. I reject and close H60 and H61. H62/R48 tests a positive TP53-loss interaction with high signature_a but gives -0.590 [-0.842,-0.338], a large interaction in the opposite direction. Thus high signature_a strongly attenuates or reverses the usual positive TP53-loss composite association. I reject H62 as stated and close it, but the evidence motivates a new reversed-direction interaction proposal to formalize attenuation/negative modification rather than accepting the original positive claim. This should be interpreted cautiously because research_signature_a is a constructed standardized assay and the threshold is an analysis-defined stratum.\n\nLineage-subtype interactions are mixed. H44/R49 suggests SMARCA4-loss is stronger in squamous than adenocarcinoma by +0.211 [+0.063,+0.359], a point estimate above threshold but lower bound below threshold, so I keep H44 unresolved and active as a potentially informative subgroup effect. H45/R50 and H46/R51 for KEAP1 and TP53 interactions are small and broad: +0.063 [-0.076,+0.202] and +0.033 [-0.184,+0.250], so they remain unresolved but deferred. H43/R52 shows media serum 10% versus 5% is null: +0.002 [-0.073,+0.076]; I reject and close it.\n\nOverall, the robust accepted core remains SMARCA4 loss associated with stronger measured dependency and KEAP1/TP53 loss associated with weaker measured dependency. PTEN loss now has accepted subgroup evidence for stronger measured dependency, especially in TP53-intact and triple-negative contexts, with independent validation requested for H58. CDKN2A appears likely below the threshold. The high research_signature_a TP53 interaction is the most striking new negative modification, and it warrants a reversed-direction interaction claim for later analysis. All conclusions remain dataset associations with a composite dependency endpoint, not single-gene causality or external generalizability.",
 "research_notes": "Updated conclusions. Validated/accepted core: SMARCA4 loss -> lower composite/stronger measured dependency; KEAP1 loss -> higher composite/weaker measured dependency; TP53 loss -> higher composite/weaker measured dependency. These three are highly separable in conditional analyses.\n\nNew PTEN conclusion: reversed PTEN-loss association is now accepted in two important contexts. H58 (TP53-intact) gives signed +0.259 CI [0.169,0.349]; H51 (triple-negative TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4 absent) gives +0.252 CI [0.169,0.335]. H59 (TP53-loss-positive) is small/unresolved: +0.102 CI [-0.187,0.391]. H50 overall reversed main remains borderline/unresolved because its own CI lower bound is below threshold, but H58/H51 support a real subgroup-specific PTEN effect. I request independent validation for H58 because it is large and addresses confounding by TP53 while retaining sample size.\n\nCDKN2A: main H19 +0.141, TP53-intact H57 +0.125, triple-negative H52 +0.144. Directionally consistent but subthreshold/uncertain; defer further work.\n\nResearch signature A interactions: high research_signature_a>=1 does not amplify SMARCA4 or KEAP1 associations (H60/H61 null). It strongly attenuates/opposes the positive TP53-loss association: H62 signed -0.590 CI [-0.842,-0.338]. Registered reversed-direction TP53-by-signature_a interaction proposal for later formalization. Do not overgeneralize because signature_a is constructed and threshold is arbitrary.\n\nLineage subtype: SMARCA4-by-squamous interaction H44 +0.211 CI [0.063,0.359] is borderline/unresolved active; KEAP1 and TP53 lineage interactions H45/H46 unresolved deferred.\n\nMedia serum 10% vs 5% H43 is null and closed.\n\nNext priorities: 1 assess validation of H58; if validated, consider whether H50 overall reversed PTEN can be accepted with careful subgroup caveat. 2 run remaining pending context interactions H47-H49 and technical audits H33-H35/H63-H64. 3 run remaining broad screens H40-H42, H53-H56. 4 keep CDKN2A deferred unless a stronger threshold-exceeding test appears. Keep all findings as dataset associations only.",
